(1423, 1, 54, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the primary target audience for PhDiZone\'s Research Coding Development Service?', '[\"Commercial software developers\",\"PhD scholars and researchers\",\"Undergraduate students\",\"Corporate IT departments\"]', '[1]', 'Remember that PhDiZone takes an \'Academic-First Approach\' - their focus is entirely on research needs, not commercial applications.', 'The document explicitly states that the service is designed exclusively for PhD scholars and researchers who need to transform their theoretical models, algorithms, and research concepts into functional code implementations.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1424, 1, 54, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which of the following is NOT a key value proposition of PhDiZone?', '[\"Academic-First Approach\",\"Publication Compliance\",\"Commercial Application Development\",\"Scientific Rigor\"]', '[2]', 'The service bridges the gap between academic theory and practical implementation specifically for research, not commercial use.', 'The document lists five key value propositions: Academic-First Approach, Publication Compliance, Scientific Rigor, Global Accessibility, and Domain Expertise. Commercial application development is explicitly excluded as the service focuses on research purposes.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1425, 1, 54, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is PhDiZone\'s mission statement focused on?', '[\"Developing commercial software products\",\"Empowering PhD scholars with publication-ready code implementations\",\"Creating educational coding tutorials\",\"Building enterprise solutions\"]', '[1]', 'Focus on the three key outcomes: research credibility, reproducible science, and accelerating publication.', 'The mission statement explicitly aims to empower PhD scholars globally with custom, publication-ready code implementations that enhance research credibility, enable reproducible science, and accelerate the path from concept to publication.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1426, 1, 54, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'How many PhD experts does PhDiZone\'s team include according to the document?', '[\"50+ PhD Experts\",\"100+ PhD Experts\",\"150+ PhD Experts\",\"200+ PhD Experts\"]', '[2]', 'The large expert team enables PhDiZone to cover multiple research disciplines with specialized knowledge.', 'The document states under Research Domain Expertise that the team includes 150+ PhD Experts who are domain specialists across multiple fields, providing deep understanding of research methodologies.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1427, 1, 54, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What critical gap does PhDiZone\'s service aim to bridge?', '[\"Gap between students and professors\",\"Gap between academic theory and practical implementation\",\"Gap between different programming languages\",\"Gap between research and industry\"]', '[1]', 'This bridging function is central to understanding the service\'s unique value - it transforms theoretical concepts into working code.', 'The service description explicitly states that it bridges the critical gap between academic theory and practical implementation, ensuring research work meets the highest standards of scientific rigor and reproducibility.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1428, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which programming language has \'Expert\' level proficiency for LaTeX according to PhDiZone?', '[\"JavaScript\",\"Java\",\"LaTeX\",\"C\\/C++\"]', '[2]', 'LaTeX expertise is crucial for academic publishing as it\'s the standard for scientific document preparation.', 'According to the programming languages table, LaTeX is listed with Expert level proficiency and is used for Scientific Document Preparation and Formula Rendering.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1429, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the minimum inline code documentation coverage standard at PhDiZone?', '[\"60%\",\"70%\",\"80%\",\"90%\"]', '[2]', 'High documentation coverage is essential for academic code as it enables reproducibility and peer review.', 'Under Code Quality Metrics, the document specifies that Documentation Coverage requires a minimum 80% inline code documentation, ensuring comprehensive code explanation.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1430, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which machine learning frameworks does PhDiZone support?', '[\"Only TensorFlow\",\"Only PyTorch and Keras\",\"TensorFlow, Keras, PyTorch, Scikit-learn, XGBoost\",\"Only Scikit-learn\"]', '[2]', 'PhDiZone supports both deep learning frameworks (TensorFlow, Keras, PyTorch) and traditional ML libraries (Scikit-learn, XGBoost).', 'The document lists all five frameworks under Specialized Frameworks & Libraries for Machine Learning, showing comprehensive coverage of major ML tools.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1431, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which IDE is specifically mentioned for statistical computing and graphics?', '[\"PyCharm\",\"RStudio\",\"Jupyter Notebook\",\"MATLAB IDE\"]', '[1]', 'Match IDEs to their primary purposes: RStudio for R/statistics, Jupyter for data science, PyCharm for Python development.', 'Under Integrated Development Environments (IDEs), RStudio is explicitly listed for statistical computing and graphics, which is the standard tool for R programming.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1432, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What code style guide does PhDiZone follow for Python?', '[\"PEP 7\",\"PEP 8\",\"PEP 9\",\"Google Style Guide\"]', '[1]', 'PEP 8 is Python\'s standard style guide; remembering \'8\' for Python helps distinguish it from other language standards.', 'The document specifies under Code Quality Metrics that Code Style adherence includes PEP 8 for Python, which is the official Python style guide.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1433, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which simulation platform is used for network simulation in computer networks research?', '[\"MATLAB Simulink\",\"AnyLogic\",\"NS2\\/NS3\",\"OMNeT++\"]', '[2]', 'NS2/NS3 are the standard tools for network research simulations, widely used in academic publications.', 'The document lists NS2/NS3 as the simulation platform for network simulation for computer networks research under Simulation Platforms.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1434, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What visualization libraries does PhDiZone use?', '[\"Only Plotly\",\"Only Matplotlib\",\"Plotly, Matplotlib, ggplot2, D3.js\",\"Only D3.js\"]', '[2]', 'The variety of visualization tools allows for both static (Matplotlib) and interactive (Plotly, D3.js) visualizations.', 'Under Specialized Frameworks & Libraries, Visualization tools include Plotly, Matplotlib, ggplot2, and D3.js, providing comprehensive visualization capabilities across different platforms.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1435, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which publication compliance standard is mentioned for reproducibility?', '[\"IEEE Standards\",\"Springer Requirements\",\"ACM Guidelines\",\"All of the above\"]', '[3]', 'PhDiZone ensures code meets requirements from all major academic publishers to maximize publication acceptance.', 'The document lists IEEE Standards, Springer Requirements, Elsevier Compliance, and ACM Guidelines under Publication Compliance Standards, showing adherence to all major academic publishers\' requirements.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1436, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the expertise level for C/C++ programming at PhDiZone?', '[\"Beginner\",\"Intermediate\",\"Advanced\",\"Expert\"]', '[2]', 'C/C++ requires Advanced (not Expert) level due to its complexity, used primarily for performance-critical applications.', 'According to the programming languages table, C/C++ is listed with Advanced level proficiency for High-performance Computing and System Programming.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1437, 1, 55, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which framework is mentioned for discrete event simulation?', '[\"NS2\\/NS3\",\"OMNeT++\",\"MATLAB Simulink\",\"AnyLogic\"]', '[1]', 'OMNeT++ specializes in discrete event simulation, particularly useful for communication networks and distributed systems.', 'Under Simulation Platforms, OMNeT++ is explicitly listed as a discrete event simulation framework used in research.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1438, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which domain includes encryption algorithm implementation?', '[\"Machine Learning & AI\",\"Cryptography & Security\",\"Data Structures & Algorithms\",\"Image Processing\"]', '[1]', 'Cryptography focuses on securing information through encryption, protocols, and security analysis.', 'Under Computer Science & Information Technology, Cryptography & Security includes encryption algorithm implementation, blockchain development, security protocol simulation, and vulnerability assessment tools.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1439, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What type of analysis is included in Bioinformatics & Life Sciences?', '[\"Financial modeling\",\"DNA sequence analysis\",\"Network simulation\",\"Control systems\"]', '[1]', 'Bioinformatics combines biology and computing, with genomics work focusing on DNA, genes, and proteins.', 'Under Genomics & Proteomics within Bioinformatics & Life Sciences, DNA sequence analysis is listed as one of the core applications along with gene expression profiling, protein structure prediction, and phylogenetic analysis.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1440, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which service category includes Monte Carlo simulations?', '[\"Algorithm Implementation Services\",\"Simulation & Modeling Services\",\"Data Analytics Services\",\"Custom Tool Development\"]', '[1]', 'Monte Carlo methods use random sampling for simulation, making them part of modeling services rather than pure algorithms.', 'Under Service Categories, Simulation & Modeling Services explicitly includes Monte Carlo simulations along with mathematical model implementation, system behavior simulation, and agent-based modeling.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1441, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What does FEA stand for in Mechanical & Civil Engineering applications?', '[\"Financial Economic Analysis\",\"Finite Element Analysis\",\"Functional Engineering Assessment\",\"Framework Execution Architecture\"]', '[1]', 'FEA is a computational method for analyzing structures by breaking them into smaller finite elements.', 'The document uses FEA as an abbreviation for Finite Element Analysis under Mechanical & Civil Engineering, which includes structural analysis simulations, heat transfer modeling, and fluid dynamics computations.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1442, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which field includes PID controller design?', '[\"Machine Learning\",\"Signal Processing\",\"Control Systems\",\"VLSI Design\"]', '[2]', 'PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) controllers are fundamental to control systems engineering.', 'Under Electronics & Electrical Engineering, Control Systems includes PID controller design, state space modeling, optimal control algorithms, and robust control systems.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1443, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What type of modeling is included in Social Sciences & Psychology data analytics?', '[\"Structural equation modeling\",\"Neural network architectures\",\"VLSI design\",\"FPGA programming\"]', '[0]', 'Structural equation modeling is specific to social sciences for analyzing complex relationships between variables.', 'Under Social Sciences & Psychology, Statistical Modeling includes structural equation modeling along with regression analysis, factor analysis, and longitudinal data analysis.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1444, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which business application includes portfolio optimization?', '[\"Operations Research\",\"Financial Modeling\",\"Data Analytics\",\"Market Research\"]', '[1]', 'Portfolio optimization is a core financial modeling technique for balancing risk and return in investments.', 'Under Business & Finance, Financial Modeling explicitly includes portfolio optimization, risk assessment algorithms, algorithmic trading systems, and market prediction models.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1445, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What service involves developing novel algorithms from research papers?', '[\"Data Analytics Services\",\"Algorithm Implementation Services\",\"Custom Tool Development\",\"Simulation Services\"]', '[1]', 'This service transforms theoretical algorithms from papers into working implementations with validation.', 'Algorithm Implementation Services specifically includes novel algorithm development from research papers, performance optimization and benchmarking, comparative analysis with existing methods, and complexity analysis.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1446, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which medical imaging application is mentioned in the document?', '[\"X-ray analysis only\",\"MRI\\/CT scan analysis\",\"Ultrasound only\",\"None of the above\"]', '[1]', 'MRI and CT are advanced medical imaging technologies requiring specialized image processing algorithms.', 'Under Medical Imaging in Bioinformatics & Life Sciences, MRI/CT scan analysis is listed along with pathological image classification, biomedical signal processing, and drug discovery algorithms.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1447, 1, 56, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What type of system modeling is included in Signal Processing?', '[\"Financial system modeling\",\"Communication system modeling\",\"Social network modeling\",\"Supply chain modeling\"]', '[1]', 'Signal processing is fundamental to communications, analyzing and transforming signals for transmission.', 'Under Signal Processing in Electronics & Electrical Engineering, communication system modeling is listed alongside digital filter design, Fourier analysis implementations, and wavelet transforms.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1448, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'How many phases are in PhDiZone\'s development process?', '[\"Four phases\",\"Five phases\",\"Six phases\",\"Seven phases\"]', '[2]', 'Remember the logical flow: Analyze → Design → Develop → Test → Document → Deploy.', 'The document outlines a Six-Phase Development Process: (1) Requirement Analysis & Feasibility Study, (2) Design & Planning, (3) Development & Implementation, (4) Testing & Validation, (5) Documentation & Training, and (6) Deployment & Support.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0);
INSERT INTO `egc_exam_questions` (`sno`, `branch_id`, `section_id`, `bank_id`, `case_study_check`, `case_study`, `option_type`, `question`, `option`, `option_answer`, `tips`, `explanation`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_by`, `updated_at`, `status`) VALUES
(1449, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the typical duration of Phase 1: Requirement Analysis & Feasibility Study?', '[\"1-2 days\",\"2-3 days\",\"3-4 days\",\"5-7 days\"]', '[0]', 'Phase 1 is the shortest phase as it focuses on planning and assessment before actual development.', 'The document specifies that Phase 1 takes 1-2 days and includes activities like initial consultation, detailed requirement documentation, technical feasibility assessment, technology stack selection, resource allocation planning, and timeline estimation.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1450, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which phase has the longest variable duration range?', '[\"Phase 2: Design & Planning\",\"Phase 3: Development & Implementation\",\"Phase 4: Testing & Validation\",\"Phase 5: Documentation & Training\"]', '[1]', 'Development duration varies most because complexity directly impacts coding time more than other phases.', 'Phase 3: Development & Implementation has a duration of 5-15 days depending on complexity, which is the widest range and reflects the variable nature of actual coding work based on project complexity.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1451, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What deliverable is NOT part of Phase 2: Design & Planning?', '[\"System design document\",\"Algorithm flowcharts\",\"Source code with documentation\",\"Testing plan\"]', '[2]', 'Design phase produces plans and diagrams; implementation phase produces actual code.', 'Phase 2 deliverables include system design document, algorithm flowcharts, data flow diagrams, testing plan, and risk mitigation strategy. Source code with documentation is a Phase 3 deliverable.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1452, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'How often are progress updates provided to clients?', '[\"Daily\",\"Weekly\",\"Bi-weekly\",\"Monthly\"]', '[1]', 'Weekly updates balance keeping clients informed without overwhelming them with excessive reporting.', 'Under Communication Protocols, Progress Updates are specified as weekly progress reports with milestone achievements, ensuring regular client engagement.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1453, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What type of meetings are held bi-weekly for complex projects?', '[\"Planning meetings\",\"Review Meetings\",\"Training sessions\",\"Audit meetings\"]', '[1]', 'Bi-weekly reviews for complex projects provide regular checkpoints without excessive meeting overhead.', 'Under Communication Protocols, Review Meetings are described as bi-weekly video conferences specifically for complex projects to ensure alignment and progress review.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1454, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which quality control checkpoint requires client approval at major milestones?', '[\"Code Review\",\"Testing Validation\",\"Client Approval\",\"Documentation Review\"]', '[2]', 'Client approval checkpoints prevent misalignment by confirming work meets expectations before proceeding.', 'Under Quality Control Checkpoints, Client Approval is explicitly listed as requiring formal approval at each major milestone, ensuring client satisfaction throughout the process.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1455, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is included in Phase 5: Documentation & Training deliverables?', '[\"Source code only\",\"Test results only\",\"Complete user documentation and video tutorials\",\"Algorithm flowcharts only\"]', '[2]', 'Phase 5 focuses on enabling users to understand and use the system independently.', 'Phase 5 deliverables specifically include complete user documentation, video tutorials, installation packages, and troubleshooting guides to ensure users can effectively use the delivered code.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1456, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What type of support is included in Phase 6: Deployment & Support?', '[\"Code development only\",\"Initial installation only\",\"Ongoing support and revision implementation if required\",\"Design services only\"]', '[2]', 'Phase 6 extends beyond delivery to ensure successful implementation and continued functionality.', 'Phase 6 includes final code delivery and installation, knowledge transfer session, post-delivery support setup, revision implementation if required, and integration assistance for research papers, indicating comprehensive ongoing support.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1457, 1, 57, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the primary contact communication method mentioned?', '[\"Video calls only\",\"Dedicated project manager\",\"Email only\",\"Phone only\"]', '[1]', 'A dedicated project manager ensures consistency and accountability throughout the project lifecycle.', 'Under Communication Protocols, Primary Contact is described as a dedicated project manager assigned to each project, providing a single point of contact for all communication.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1458, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target documentation coverage in source code packages?', '[\"60% coverage\",\"70% coverage\",\"80% coverage\",\"90% coverage\"]', '[2]', '80% documentation coverage is a quality standard that balances thoroughness with practicality.', 'Under Source Code Package deliverables, comprehensive inline documentation is specified with a minimum 80% coverage, ensuring code is well-documented for understanding and reproducibility.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1459, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What does PhDiZone guarantee about template usage?', '[\"Templates are occasionally used\",\"Templates are used for efficiency\",\"Zero Template Reuse - all code developed from scratch\",\"Templates are preferred\"]', '[2]', 'Zero template reuse is critical for academic integrity and prevents plagiarism concerns in research.', 'Under Academic Integrity Standards, Zero Template Reuse is explicitly stated, confirming that all code is developed from scratch for each project to ensure originality and academic integrity.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1460, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What operating systems does PhDiZone support for multi-platform compatibility?', '[\"Windows only\",\"macOS only\",\"Windows, macOS, Linux\",\"Linux only\"]', '[2]', 'Cross-platform support is essential for research code as researchers use varied computing environments.', 'Under Multi-Platform Compatibility, Operating Systems explicitly lists Windows, macOS, and Linux compatibility, ensuring code works across all major platforms.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1461, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What version control system is used at PhDiZone?', '[\"SVN\",\"Mercurial\",\"Git-based version management\",\"CVS\"]', '[2]', 'Git is the standard version control system in research and development for tracking code changes.', 'Under Multi-Platform Compatibility, Version Control is specified as Git-based version management, which is the industry standard for modern code versioning.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1462, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is emphasized for performance optimization?', '[\"Only algorithm efficiency\",\"Only memory management\",\"Algorithm efficiency, memory management, parallel processing, and scalability\",\"Only code readability\"]', '[2]', 'Comprehensive performance optimization addresses multiple dimensions: speed, memory, parallelization, and scale.', 'Under Performance Optimization, all four aspects are listed: Algorithm Efficiency, Memory Management, Parallel Processing (multi-threading and GPU acceleration), and Scalability for handling large datasets.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1463, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the advantage of PhDiZone\'s India-based team?', '[\"Higher cost\",\"Limited availability\",\"Cost-effective development with high-quality output\",\"Language barriers\"]', '[2]', 'Geographic location provides cost advantages while maintaining quality through expert team and global standards.', 'Under Global Reach with Local Expertise, the India-Based Team is described as providing cost-effective development with high-quality output, combined with global standards and 24/7 support across time zones.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1464, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What test coverage target is specified for unit testing?', '[\"Greater than 70%\",\"Greater than 80%\",\"Greater than 90%\",\"100%\"]', '[2]', '90%+ test coverage is a high standard that ensures almost all code paths are tested for reliability.', 'Under Technical Quality Standards, Test Coverage is specified as comprehensive unit testing with greater than 90% coverage, ensuring thorough testing of all code functions.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1465, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'How is intellectual property handled in PhDiZone projects?', '[\"Shared ownership\",\"PhDiZone retains ownership\",\"Complete ownership transfer to the scholar\",\"University ownership only\"]', '[2]', 'Full IP transfer is crucial for researchers to publish and use their code without restrictions.', 'Under Academic Integrity Standards, Intellectual Property Protection explicitly states complete ownership transfer to the scholar, ensuring researchers retain full rights to their work.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1466, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What type of code complexity is maintained according to quality standards?', '[\"High cyclomatic complexity\",\"Variable complexity\",\"Low cyclomatic complexity - maintainable code\",\"Unrestricted complexity\"]', '[2]', 'Low cyclomatic complexity means fewer decision points, making code easier to understand and maintain.', 'Under Technical Quality Standards, Code Complexity is specified as maintainable code with low cyclomatic complexity, ensuring code is understandable and maintainable.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1467, 1, 58, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What cloud deployment options are available?', '[\"AWS only\",\"Google Cloud only\",\"AWS\\/Google Cloud deployment options\",\"No cloud options\"]', '[2]', 'Supporting multiple cloud providers gives researchers flexibility based on their institutional resources.', 'Under Multi-Platform Compatibility, Cloud Deployment explicitly mentions AWS/Google Cloud deployment options, providing flexibility in cloud platform choice.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1468, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the pricing range for Interactive Visualization Dashboard add-on?', '[\"10-15% of base cost\",\"15-25% of base cost\",\"20-30% of base cost\",\"30-50% of base cost\"]', '[2]', 'Visualization dashboards add moderate cost because they require additional development for interactive interfaces.', 'The Interactive Visualization Dashboard add-on service is priced at an additional 20-30% of base project cost with a timeline of 3-5 additional days.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1469, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What technologies are used for the Interactive Visualization Dashboard?', '[\"Only Python libraries\",\"Plotly, Dash, Streamlit, D3.js, Matplotlib\",\"Only MATLAB\",\"Only R packages\"]', '[1]', 'The mix of technologies enables both interactive web-based (Dash, D3.js) and Python-based (Plotly, Matplotlib) visualizations.', 'The dashboard service explicitly lists these technologies: Plotly, Dash, Streamlit, D3.js, and Matplotlib, providing comprehensive visualization capabilities across web and desktop platforms.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1470, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the expected performance improvement from Code Optimization & Performance Tuning?', '[\"Up to 30-40%\",\"Up to 40-60%\",\"Up to 50-80%\",\"Up to 60-90%\"]', '[2]', 'Optimization can dramatically improve performance by focusing on algorithm complexity, memory, and parallel processing.', 'Under the benefits of Code Optimization & Performance Tuning, the service promises up to 50-80% performance improvement along with reduced computational resource requirements.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1471, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the pricing for Scalability Enhancement services?', '[\"15-25% additional\",\"20-30% additional\",\"25-40% additional\",\"30-50% additional\"]', '[3]', 'Scalability is expensive because it involves fundamental architecture changes for distributed computing.', 'Scalability Enhancement is priced at an additional 30-50% of base project cost, which is one of the higher add-on costs due to the complexity of distributed computing implementation.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1472, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is included in the Model Packaging & Containerization service?', '[\"Source code only\",\"Containerized execution environment and one-click deployment scripts\",\"Documentation only\",\"Testing scripts only\"]', '[1]', 'Containerization ensures code runs identically across different environments, solving the \'it works on my machine\' problem.', 'The service features include containerized execution environment, one-click deployment scripts, cross-platform compatibility, version control integration, and automatic dependency management.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1473, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'How much does the LaTeX Integration & Scientific Writing Support service cost?', '[\"5-10% additional\",\"10-15% additional\",\"15-20% additional\",\"20-25% additional\"]', '[1]', 'LaTeX integration is relatively low-cost because it primarily involves formatting existing results for publication.', 'LaTeX Integration & Scientific Writing Support is priced at an additional 10-15% of base project cost with a timeline of 1-2 additional days.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1474, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the timeline for Research Paper Writing Based on Implementation service?', '[\"5-10 additional days\",\"10-15 additional days\",\"15-30 additional days\",\"30-45 additional days\"]', '[2]', 'Full paper writing takes significantly longer as it involves research, writing, and multiple revision cycles.', 'Research Paper Writing Based on Implementation has a timeline of 15-30 additional days and requires separate service pricing (contact for details), reflecting the comprehensive nature of full paper writing.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1475, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What bug fix period is included in Standard Support?', '[\"15 days post-delivery\",\"30 days post-delivery\",\"60 days post-delivery\",\"90 days post-delivery\"]', '[1]', '30-day bug fix coverage is standard practice, covering issues discovered during initial use.', 'Standard Support (Included) provides free bug fixes for 30 days post-delivery, along with email support within 24 hours, basic queries assistance, and documentation access.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1476, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the response time for Priority Support email and chat?', '[\"Within 2 hours\",\"Within 4 hours\",\"Within 8 hours\",\"Within 24 hours\"]', '[1]', 'Priority support offers 6x faster response (4 vs 24 hours) for researchers with urgent needs.', 'Priority Support (Add-on) specifies email & chat support with response within 4 hours, compared to 24 hours for standard support, along with extended 90-day bug fixes and phone support.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1477, 1, 59, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What warranty period is included in Premium Support?', '[\"3 months\",\"4 months\",\"6 months\",\"12 months\"]', '[2]', 'Premium support extends coverage from 30/90 days to 6 months, ideal for long-term research projects.', 'Premium Support (Add-on) includes Extended Warranty with free updates and fixes for 6 months, along with 24/7 support, dedicated support contact, and video consultations.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1478, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target delivery timeline success rate?', '[\"Greater than 85%\",\"Greater than 90%\",\"Greater than 95%\",\"100%\"]', '[2]', '95%+ on-time delivery is an exceptionally high standard showing strong project management.', 'Under Client Satisfaction metrics, Delivery Timeline is specified as greater than 95% on-time delivery rate, demonstrating PhDiZone\'s commitment to meeting deadlines.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1479, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target bug rate per 1000 lines of code?', '[\"Less than 3 bugs\",\"Less than 5 bugs\",\"Less than 10 bugs\",\"Less than 15 bugs\"]', '[1]', 'Less than 5 bugs per 1000 lines indicates high-quality code with thorough testing and review.', 'Under Code Quality metrics, Bug Rate is specified as less than 5 bugs per 1000 lines of code, which is an industry-leading quality standard.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1480, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target client quality rating?', '[\"Average rating greater than 3.5\\/5.0\",\"Average rating greater than 4.0\\/5.0\",\"Average rating greater than 4.5\\/5.0\",\"Average rating greater than 4.8\\/5.0\"]', '[2]', '4.5/5.0 rating means 90% satisfaction, demonstrating consistently high-quality service delivery.', 'Under Client Satisfaction, Quality Rating target is specified as average client rating greater than 4.5/5.0, indicating high client satisfaction.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1481, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What percentage of codes should be used in successful publications?', '[\"Greater than 70%\",\"Greater than 80%\",\"Greater than 90%\",\"100%\"]', '[2]', '90%+ publication success validates that code meets rigorous academic standards for research papers.', 'Under Client Satisfaction, Publication Success is measured as greater than 90% of codes used in successful publications, demonstrating the publication-ready quality of delivered work.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1482, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target project success rate?', '[\"Greater than 95%\",\"Greater than 96%\",\"Greater than 97%\",\"Greater than 98%\"]', '[3]', '98%+ success rate indicates robust processes and experienced team minimizing project failures.', 'Under Operational Excellence, Project Success Rate is specified as greater than 98% successful project completion, demonstrating exceptional execution capability.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1483, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target for projects requiring major revisions?', '[\"Less than 10%\",\"Less than 15%\",\"Less than 20%\",\"Less than 25%\"]', '[2]', 'Less than 20% major revisions means 80%+ of projects meet expectations without significant rework.', 'Under Client Satisfaction, Revision Rate is specified as less than 20% of projects require major revisions, indicating high first-time quality.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
(1484, 1, 60, 15, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target client retention rate?', '[\"Greater than 70%\",\"Greater than 75%\",\"Greater than 80%\",\"Greater than 85%\"]', '[2]', '80%+ retention indicates clients are satisfied enough to return for future projects.', 'Under Operational Excellence, Client Retention is measured as greater than 80% client return rate for additional projects, showing strong relationship building.', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 1, '2025-10-09 07:58:08', 0),
