(1499, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the typical word count range for Original Research papers?', '[\"4,000-6,000 words\",\"5,000-7,000 words\",\"6,000-8,000 words\",\"8,000-12,000 words\"]', '[2]', 'Original Research is the longest category except for Review Papers - both are \'High\' complexity.', 'Original Research papers, which are novel empirical studies with original data, typically range from 6,000-8,000 words and are classified as High complexity level.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1500, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the complexity level of Case Studies?', '[\"Low\",\"Low-Medium\",\"Medium\",\"High\"]', '[2]', 'Case Studies and Conceptual Papers both have Medium complexity - they\'re in the middle range.', 'Case Studies, which provide in-depth analysis of specific instances, are classified as Medium complexity level with typical lengths of 4,000-6,000 words.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1501, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which manuscript category has the longest typical word count?', '[\"Original Research\",\"Review Papers\",\"Conceptual Papers\",\"Case Studies\"]', '[1]', 'Review Papers = longest word count because they synthesize extensive existing literature.', 'Review Papers, which are systematic or narrative literature reviews, have the longest typical length at 8,000-12,000 words and High complexity level.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1502, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the word count range for Short Communications?', '[\"1,000-2,000 words\",\"2,000-3,000 words\",\"3,000-4,000 words\",\"4,000-5,000 words\"]', '[1]', 'Short Communications are the briefest category - perfect for quick, focused findings.', 'Short Communications, which present brief research findings, typically range from 2,000-3,000 words with Low-Medium complexity level.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1503, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which formatting style is used for Engineering and Computer Science disciplines?', '[\"APA\",\"IEEE\",\"MLA\",\"Chicago\"]', '[1]', 'IEEE = Engineering - both start with \'E\' to help remember the connection.', 'IEEE formatting style is used for Engineering and Computer Science disciplines, featuring numbered references and specific citation format.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1504, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which citation style uses an author-date system for Psychology and Social Sciences?', '[\"MLA\",\"APA\",\"Chicago\",\"Vancouver\"]', '[1]', 'APA = Psychology - remember \'American Psychological Association\' for easy recall.', 'APA (American Psychological Association) style uses an author-date system with comprehensive guidelines and is primarily used for Psychology and Social Sciences.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1505, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which formatting style uses a numerical sequence system for Medical/Life Sciences?', '[\"Harvard\",\"APA\",\"Vancouver\",\"MLA\"]', '[2]', 'Vancouver is numerical like medical charts - sequential and precise.', 'Vancouver style uses a numerical sequence system and is the standard for Medical and Life Sciences publications.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1506, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which journal classification represents Web of Science indexed publications?', '[\"Scopus Q1-Q4\",\"SCI\\/SCI-E\",\"IEEE Xplore\",\"SpringerLink\"]', '[1]', 'SCI = Science Citation Index = Web of Science - all about citation tracking.', 'SCI/SCI-E (Science Citation Index/Science Citation Index Expanded) represents Web of Science indexed publications, which are high-impact journals.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1507, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What does the \'Q\' in Scopus Q1-Q4 represent?', '[\"Quality tier\",\"Quartile ranking\",\"Quick review\",\"Qualified journal\"]', '[1]', 'Quartile divides journals into four equal groups - Q1 is top tier, Q4 is lowest.', 'Scopus Q1-Q4 represents quartile-based journal rankings, with Q1 being the top 25% of journals in a category and Q4 being the bottom quartile.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1508, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which database indexing is specifically for Indian academic recognition?', '[\"Web of Science\",\"Scopus Database\",\"PubMed\",\"UGC-Care\"]', '[3]', 'UGC-Care is India-specific - \'UGC\' stands for University Grants Commission of India.', 'UGC-Care (University Grants Commission - Career Advancement Recognition) is specifically for Indian academic recognition and promotion purposes.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1509, 1, 62, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which citation style uses an author-page format for Humanities and Literature?', '[\"APA\",\"IEEE\",\"MLA\",\"Vancouver\"]', '[2]', 'MLA = Literature - Modern Language Association focuses on language and literature.', 'MLA (Modern Language Association) style uses an author-page format with works cited, primarily for Humanities and Literature disciplines.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1510, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'How many stages are in PhDiZone\'s Publication Pipeline?', '[\"5 stages\",\"6 stages\",\"7 stages\",\"8 stages\"]', '[2]', '7 stages = complete week - each stage is a systematic step toward publication success.', 'PhDiZone follows a comprehensive 7-Stage Publication Pipeline, from Manuscript Assessment & Intake through Post-Publication Support.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1511, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the duration of Stage 1: Manuscript Assessment & Intake?', '[\"1 business day\",\"1-2 business days\",\"2-3 business days\",\"3-5 business days\"]', '[1]', 'Stage 1 is the quickest stage - just initial assessment and intake.', 'Stage 1 involves initial manuscript review, plagiarism screening, technical feasibility assessment, and client consultation, completed within 1-2 business days.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1512, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which stage includes comprehensive editing by domain experts?', '[\"Stage 1: Manuscript Assessment\",\"Stage 2: Technical & Language Enhancement\",\"Stage 3: Journal Selection\",\"Stage 4: Submission Preparation\"]', '[1]', 'Stage 2 = Enhancement - this is where manuscripts get polished by experts.', 'Stage 2 includes comprehensive editing by domain experts, language polishing, structural improvements, and citation verification, taking 5-7 business days.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1513, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the duration of Stage 3: Journal Selection & Targeting?', '[\"1-2 business days\",\"2-3 business days\",\"3-5 business days\",\"5-7 business days\"]', '[1]', 'Stage 3 is short because it focuses on strategic selection, not content revision.', 'Stage 3 involves impact factor analysis, scope matching, publication timeline assessment, and cost-benefit analysis, completed in 2-3 business days.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1514, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which stage includes metadata and keyword optimization?', '[\"Stage 2: Technical Enhancement\",\"Stage 3: Journal Selection\",\"Stage 4: Submission Preparation\",\"Stage 5: Peer Review Management\"]', '[2]', 'Stage 4 = Submission prep - everything needed to submit, including SEO optimization.', 'Stage 4 includes final formatting, cover letter preparation, metadata and keyword optimization, and submission portal management, taking 3-5 business days.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1515, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the variable duration of Stage 5: Peer Review Management?', '[\"1-3 months\",\"1-6 months\",\"3-9 months\",\"6-12 months\"]', '[1]', 'Peer review is the longest and most variable stage - depends entirely on the journal\'s process.', 'Stage 5 duration is variable, lasting 1-6 months based on the journal, and includes review status monitoring, reviewer comment analysis, and revision implementation.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1516, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the duration of Stage 6: Acceptance & Final Processing?', '[\"1-2 weeks\",\"2-4 weeks\",\"4-6 weeks\",\"6-8 weeks\"]', '[1]', '2-4 weeks post-acceptance = final quality checks before official publication.', 'Stage 6 occurs post-acceptance and takes 2-4 weeks, including proof checking, APC processing assistance, final publication verification, and citation tracking setup.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1517, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which stage has an \'ongoing as needed\' duration?', '[\"Stage 5: Peer Review Management\",\"Stage 6: Acceptance & Final Processing\",\"Stage 7: Post-Publication Support\",\"Stage 4: Submission Preparation\"]', '[2]', 'Stage 7 never truly ends - PhDiZone provides continuous support even after publication.', 'Stage 7: Post-Publication Support is ongoing as needed and includes publication certificate provision, impact tracking, future publication consultation, and researcher profile enhancement.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1518, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What plagiarism similarity threshold does PhDiZone maintain?', '[\"\\u22645%\",\"\\u226410%\",\"\\u226415%\",\"\\u226420%\"]', '[1]', '10% or less similarity = acceptable academic standard for originality.', 'PhDiZone maintains a strict plagiarism threshold of ≤10% similarity, verified using iThenticate/Turnitin plagiarism detection tools.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1519, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which tools does PhDiZone use for plagiarism checking?', '[\"Grammarly and Copyscape\",\"iThenticate and Turnitin\",\"Plagscan and Quetext\",\"PlagScan and Duplichecker\"]', '[1]', 'iThenticate and Turnitin are the gold standards for academic plagiarism detection.', 'PhDiZone uses industry-standard tools iThenticate and Turnitin for plagiarism detection, ensuring manuscripts meet the ≤10% similarity criterion.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1520, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What standard must language quality meet according to PhDiZone\'s quality checkpoints?', '[\"Academic English standard\",\"Native English standard\",\"Professional English standard\",\"Advanced English standard\"]', '[1]', 'Native English standard = publication-ready quality, not just grammatically correct.', 'PhDiZone ensures manuscripts meet Native English standards through editing by PhD-level editors, ensuring clarity and academic tone.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1521, 1, 63, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the journal compliance criterion in PhDiZone\'s quality checkpoints?', '[\"90% guideline adherence\",\"95% guideline adherence\",\"100% guideline adherence\",\"Best effort guideline adherence\"]', '[2]', '100% compliance is non-negotiable - even small deviations can lead to desk rejection.', 'PhDiZone ensures 100% guideline adherence through automated and manual checks, guaranteeing manuscripts meet all journal requirements.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1522, 1, 64, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which primary service focuses on high-impact reference integration?', '[\"Technical Editing\",\"Language Polishing\",\"Citation Enhancement\",\"Structural Optimization\"]', '[2]', 'Strong citations = stronger manuscript - this service adds academic credibility.', 'Citation Enhancement is a component of Manuscript Development & Enhancement that focuses on high-impact reference integration to strengthen the manuscript\'s scholarly foundation.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:43', 0),
(1523, 1, 64, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What does Impact Factor Analysis help determine in Journal Selection & Targeting?', '[\"Manuscript quality\",\"Research scope with journal reputation\",\"Author credentials\",\"Submission fees\"]', '[1]', 'Impact factor = journal prestige - higher impact = more competitive but more prestigious.', 'Impact Factor Analysis matches the research scope with journal reputation to identify the most appropriate and prestigious publication venues.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:44', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:44', 0),
(1524, 1, 64, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'Which service provides expert rebuttal and revision support?', '[\"Portal Navigation\",\"Review Response\",\"Timeline Tracking\",\"Resubmission Support\"]', '[1]', 'Strong rebuttals can turn rejection into acceptance - expert support is crucial here.', 'Review Response service provides expert rebuttal and revision support, helping authors effectively address reviewer comments and improve acceptance chances.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:44', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:44', 0),
(1525, 1, 64, 16, 0, NULL, 0, 'What is the target benefit of Native Proofreading add-on service?', '[\"Faster submission\",\"Publication-ready quality\",\"Lower costs\",\"Higher impact factor\"]', '[1]', 'Native proofreading is the final polish - makes the difference between good and excellent.', 'Native Proofreading provides advanced language enhancement by PhD editors to achieve publication-ready quality that meets journal standards.', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:44', 1, '2025-10-09 08:03:44', 0),
